  "fixes_during_release": [
    "Restored default server settings and base map rotations; excluded test credentials and fixed the feasibility helper symlink overwrite.",
    "Restored Katabatic base distribution and regenerated the offline asset manifest/bundle.",
    "Built shutdown patches for every client platform, including portable Linux Steam Audio.",
    "Added Linux-only bot worker archive, notices and package audits.",
    "Updated the weapon-cache regression to compare the complete uncached presentation.",
    "Prevented stale enemy dereferences in native and scripted bot steering/Assault targeting; added a disappearing-target differential regression after a real worker crash during human departure.",
    "Excluded generated Godot import sidecars from Android runtime resource compilation."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No fresh physical VR headset or vest test during release preparation. Windows and Quest are cross-built/package-verified; rendered runtime smoke tests use Linux.",
    "Bot-worker transport was tested locally, not over WAN. Katabatic navigation can still leave bots stuck; offloading is not a route repair.",
    "Fixture-only malformed audio/packet and dummy-renderer material diagnostics may appear in regression logs. Final rendered-client, server and worker integration logs contain no runtime errors.",
    "Original patch context whitespace and third-party credit file formatting are preserved.",
    "Final archives are gated by tools/prepare_release.py; published BUILD-MANIFEST.json and SHA256SUMS identify the commit and exact uploaded bytes."
  ]
